    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9370" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">com-mīlĭtĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n.
		militia, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>companionship in war</i> (prob. not in use before
			the Aug. period). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Prop., Veil. 2, 29, 5; * <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				10, 111</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 1, 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 4, 4,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 5, 10, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 5, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				10, 11, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
				18, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>fellowship</i>,
				<i>companionship</i> in gen. (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(studiorum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 2, 5, 72</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. Flor. 3, p. 356, 1</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Manil. 1, 780</span></i>.</div>
